<h2><strong><span style="font-size: 20px; color: #1a1d28;">Binance Historical Ticker Data</span></strong></h2>
<p><span style="color: #1a1d28;">We provide Historical and live </span><a href="https://docs.amberdata.io/docs/tickers-1"><span>best bid and best ask</span></a><span style="color: #1a1d28;"> (top of the books) for any traded instrument, as well as incremental tick-level updates/deltas of all bids and asks on an order book. This level 2 data is available within the Order Book endpoints. From this tick-level order book data, we are able to derive Tickers, which is simply the best bid and best ask (top of the order books) for a traded instrument.</span></p>
<p><span style="color: #1a1d28;">Our spot data for Binance goes back to 2017-08-17; for Binance futures, 2021-04-12; and for Binance.US spot, 2022-06-15.</span></p>
<p><span style="color: #1a1d28;">Our Tickers endpoints are available via REST API for historical (time series) data as well as WebSockets for real-time data.</span></p>
<p><span style="color: #1a1d28;">Here is a </span><a href="https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1VuzUvJDHFSNPHu5I-fWunOxoKk6V24zWcUwLN628t7E/edit#gid=1818969799"><span>sample file</span></a><span style="color: #1a1d28;">.</span></p>
